/-
# Finite bases of identities of finite algebras (Kourovka Notebook Problem 2.41)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.41 (A. I. Mal'cev): is the variety
generated by (a) a finite associative ring, (b) a finite Lie ring, (c) a finite quasigroup finitely
axiomatizable? (d) What is the cardinality `n` of the smallest semigroup generating a
non-finitely-axiomatizable variety?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Order.Bounds.Defs
public import Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite
public import WantedExt.Algebra.VarietyIdentitiesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Algebra.FiniteAlgebraFiniteBasisKourovka2Problem41Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.41 (A. I.
Mal'cev). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700114 (`KOU-2.41`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A variety is represented through the identities of an algebra: the variety generated by an algebra
is finitely based exactly when finitely many of its identities imply all of them in every algebra of
the signature (all algebras in `Type`), and a variety is finitely based exactly when the algebra
generating it (its free algebra of countable rank) has this property. Group words are elements of
`FreeGroup ℕ`; ring identities are elements of the free non-unital associative ring `MonoidAlgebra ℤ
(FreeSemigroup ℕ)` (associative rings are not assumed unital, the convention of the Mal'cev school
and of the Specht problem); Lie ring identities are elements of the free Lie ring `FreeLieAlgebra ℤ
ℕ`. These definitions are shared with the other varieties entries in
`WantedExt.Algebra.VarietyIdentitiesShared`. Quasigroups are equational quasigroups in the signature
`(·, \, /)`, with terms over `x₀, x₁, …` given by the inductive type `QTerm`; semigroup identities
are pairs of words in `FreeSemigroup ℕ`. Part (d) is stated as `6` being the least cardinality of a
finite semigroup (the empty one included, which is finitely based) whose variety is not finitely
based.
-/

open MathlibExt.Algebra.VarietyIdentitiesShared

/-- Kourovka 2.41(a) (A. I. Mal'cev): the variety generated by a finite associative ring is
finitely based. -/
def finiteRingVarietyFinitelyBased : Prop :=
  ∀ (A : Type) [NonUnitalRing A] [Finite A], RingIdentitiesFinitelyBased A

/-- Kourovka 2.41(b): the variety generated by a finite Lie ring is finitely based. -/
def finiteLieRingVarietyFinitelyBased : Prop :=
  ∀ (L : Type) [LieRing L] [Finite L], LieIdentitiesFinitelyBased L

/-- Terms in the quasigroup signature (multiplication `·`, left division `\`, right division `/`)
over the variables `x₀, x₁, …`. -/
inductive QTerm
  | var : ℕ → QTerm
  | mul : QTerm → QTerm → QTerm
  | ldiv : QTerm → QTerm → QTerm
  | rdiv : QTerm → QTerm → QTerm

/-- An algebra of the quasigroup signature on `Q`: multiplication, left and right division. -/
abbrev QOps (Q : Type) := (Q → Q → Q) × (Q → Q → Q) × (Q → Q → Q)

/-- The value of a term under the assignment `x : ℕ → Q`. -/
def QTerm.eval {Q : Type} (o : QOps Q) (x : ℕ → Q) : QTerm → Q
  | .var i => x i
  | .mul s t => o.1 (s.eval o x) (t.eval o x)
  | .ldiv s t => o.2.1 (s.eval o x) (t.eval o x)
  | .rdiv s t => o.2.2 (s.eval o x) (t.eval o x)

/-- The algebra is an (equational) quasigroup: `a \ (a b) = b`, `a (a \ b) = b`,
`(a b) / b = a` and `(a / b) b = a`. -/
def QOps.IsQuasigroup {Q : Type} (o : QOps Q) : Prop :=
  ∀ a b : Q, o.2.1 a (o.1 a b) = b ∧ o.1 a (o.2.1 a b) = b ∧ o.2.2 (o.1 a b) b = a ∧
    o.1 (o.2.2 a b) b = a

/-- The algebra satisfies the identity `e.1 = e.2`. -/
def QOps.Satisfies {Q : Type} (o : QOps Q) (e : QTerm × QTerm) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : ℕ → Q, e.1.eval o x = e.2.eval o x

/-- The variety generated by the algebra is finitely based: finitely many of its identities imply
all of them in every algebra of the signature. -/
def QOps.FinitelyBased {Q : Type} (o : QOps Q) : Prop :=
  ∃ B : Finset (QTerm × QTerm), (∀ e ∈ B, o.Satisfies e) ∧
    ∀ (P : Type) (p : QOps P), (∀ e ∈ B, p.Satisfies e) → ∀ e, o.Satisfies e → p.Satisfies e

/-- Kourovka 2.41(c): the variety generated by a finite quasigroup is finitely based. -/
def finiteQuasigroupVarietyFinitelyBased : Prop :=
  ∀ (Q : Type) [Finite Q] (o : QOps Q), o.IsQuasigroup → o.FinitelyBased

/-- The semigroup `S` satisfies the identity `e.1 = e.2` between words in `x₀, x₁, …`. -/
def SemigroupSatisfies (S : Type) [Semigroup S] (e : FreeSemigroup ℕ × FreeSemigroup ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : ℕ → S, FreeSemigroup.lift x e.1 = FreeSemigroup.lift x e.2

/-- The variety generated by the semigroup `S` is finitely based. -/
def SemigroupFinitelyBased (S : Type) [Semigroup S] : Prop :=
  ∃ B : Finset (FreeSemigroup ℕ × FreeSemigroup ℕ), (∀ e ∈ B, SemigroupSatisfies S e) ∧
    ∀ (T : Type) [Semigroup T], (∀ e ∈ B, SemigroupSatisfies T e) →
      ∀ e, SemigroupSatisfies S e → SemigroupSatisfies T e

/-- Kourovka 2.41(d): the least cardinality of a finite semigroup generating a variety that is not
finitely based is `6`. -/
def leastOrderNonFinitelyBasedSemigroup : Prop :=
  IsLeast {n : ℕ | ∃ (S : Type) (_ : Semigroup S), Finite S ∧ Nat.card S = n ∧
    ¬ SemigroupFinitelyBased S} 6

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.41(a) "Yes" (L'vov; Kruse, 1973): the variety
generated by a finite associative ring has a finite basis of identities (Drensky's survey, Theorem
4.1). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The
Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.41
(A. I. Mal'cev); resolution: I. V. L'vov, Algebra and Logic 12 (1973), 156-167; R. L. Kruse, J.
Algebra 26 (1973), 298-318; Yu. A. Bakhturin and A. Yu. Ol'shanskii, Math. USSR-Sb. 25 (1975),
507-523; M. R. Vaughan-Lee, Algebra Universalis 9 (1979), 269-280; P. Perkins, J. Algebra 11 (1969),
298-314; A. N. Trakhtman, Semigroup Forum 27 (1983), 387-389; survey: V. Drensky, Finite basis
problem for varieties of algebraic systems, arXiv:2602.18805 (2026), Kourovka Archive, Problem 2.41:
a) Yes; b) Yes; c) Not always; d) n = 6; Drensky's survey, Theorem 4.1 (varieties generated by
finite associative rings, Kruse and L'vov, and by finite Lie rings, Bahturin-Ol'shanskii, are
finitely based), Theorem 6.2 (Perkins's six-element semigroup is not finitely based) and Theorem 6.3
(Trahtman: every semigroup with at most 5 elements is finitely based),
https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.18805.
-/
public theorem_wanted finiteRingVarietyFinitelyBased_holds : finiteRingVarietyFinitelyBased

